WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:09.750
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:20.380
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.500
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:06.980
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:14.280
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.990
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:28.180
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.770
Neviril, more… More powerful, Neviril.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.940
Neviril, don’t look! You can’t
kill them if you see their eyes!

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.530
Neviril!

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.430
Amuria!

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.520
Amuria!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:15.420
<b>Wounds and Pain</b>

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:25.780
Hey, Alty. Chase those birds. Please?

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.600
We’re on duty right now, you know.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.650
So what? We won’t
run into the enemy here!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.850
You’ll just miss out
if you’re so wound up.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:38.980
Well, I guess you’re
right about that, but…

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:46.100
They’ve been flying by us awhile.
I wonder where they’re headed.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.270
They can’t fly forever. They’ll rest
their wings when they’re tired.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.820
They’ve got to eat
when they get hungry, right?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.200
What are they doing? We’re on duty.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.180
Things seem pretty
mellow these days.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:14.000
I guess so.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.300
We finally returned to duty too.
We seem to have lost our edge.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.990
And Aer never
volunteers to fly anymore…

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.200
Para-sama…

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.240
How’s Sibylla Aurea
doing these days?

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.710
The same, huh?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.000
Are you concerned?

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.750
Not really.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.460
But it’s like we’ve been left hanging.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.010
It seems like the others are
starting to accept her being gone.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:51.020
This means we can never go back
to the old Chor Tempest, doesn’t it?

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.630
Para-sama…

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:57.980
I’m keeping
an eye on you, Para-sama.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.860
Just kidding.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.910
Rimone,
we’re heading for the pool now.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.810
I’m not.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:12.830
No.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.650
You’re still young, so your endurance…

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.790
I’m hungry!

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.580
Rimone! Hey, hold on!

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.920
Um, why don’t we all take lunch first?

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.940
Is something the matter,
Sibylla Paraietta?

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.160
This is Sibylla Aurea’s…

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.150
I’m still repairing it.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.520
We had to rebuild
some things from scratch…

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:51.450
…so I had a hard time
getting all the components.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.330
Your wounds haven’t healed yet.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.710
You haven’t flown in a while.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.650
Neviril! Hey, Neviril!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.980
You’ve been cooped up long enough.
Get back on duty already!

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:34.660
Chor Tempest just gets lame missions
because you won’t come back!

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.400
I can’t take much more!

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.920
This is no place for us to be flying!

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.670
Are you listening, Neviril?

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.540
Neviril!

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:58.060
You stubborn mule!

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.370
Really, what a childish thing…

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.090
I guess I’m in no position to talk.

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:44.940
I’m sorry. There was
no need for you to do that.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.770
No, I really didn’t mind.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:50.750
Really, what are
we going to do with Aer?

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:53.280
She’s troubling you, right?
Shall I make her stop?

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:00.840
Of course, I’m sure
it’s not going to be pretty…

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.510
Neviril… Don’t you think
it’s time you made things clear?

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.230
Made what clear?

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:17.800
Either way, we can’t go on like this.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.490
Won’t you come back to the chor?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:28.050
If you decide to go to the Spring,
then this time I’ll accompany you.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:29.170
I’m sorry.

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:34.690
I’m still unsure myself.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.200
About going to the Spring…
and about flying Simouns.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.060
I can’t decide yet.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.430
But…

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:44.040
I’m fully aware that it’s wrong.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:51.240
But I feel that no matter which choice
I make, it would be a betrayal…

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:52.600
Betrayal?

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.430
That’s the feeling I get.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.560
You mean Amuria.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:15.220
Neviril… I’ve spent my life by your
side ever since we were children.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.160
I’ve always walked
the same path as you.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.420
That’s why I can say this.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.620
Your place is in a Simoun.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:31.210
Even if that means
you’ll have to betray Amuria…

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.710
Don’t talk to me as if you know!

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:38.340
It’s not as simple as that.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.730
Leave me.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.000
I see…

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.140
She’s overwhelmed, huh?

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:10.140
And you’ve been so worried
about her, Para-sama…

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:26.890
But I don’t see why she doesn’t
try to understand how you feel.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:29.580
I don’t like the way Neviril’s acting.

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:31.960
Don’t talk like you know.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.630
I do know.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.550
In other words,
she’s just being childish, right?

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:40.610
She’s not.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:42.010
Then what’s up with her?

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.290
Sure, losing Amuria
was a big blow to her…

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:59.730
…but she’s not
the only one who misses her.

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:04.450
Keeping herself holed up is really
causing trouble for the rest of us.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.450
Kaim.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:11.460
I’m sorry. I was out of line.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.670
Para-sama.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.610
What happened to your hands?

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.210
Oh, I was cleaning something…

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.300
You can’t just leave them like that.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.220
I know! Could you wait a little?

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.340
S-Sure.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:37.000
I see… My nails are starting to shine.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.060
Aren’t they? You’ve got such beautiful
fingers, so take care of them…

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:43.360
…or Tempus Spatium will scold you.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.750
You enjoy this.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:53.070
I’m getting to take care of you, aren’t I?

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.750
And touch you.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:57.750
Just kidding.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:05.850
I think she’s just lonely.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.460
We probably all are.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.220
All of us on this ship…

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:16.230
Lonely, probably… That’s what I think.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.320
I’m sorry.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.240
Hey, Para-sama.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.450
Are you lonely too, Para-sama?

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:38.440
Do I look that bad to you?

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.130
That’s not what I meant.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.510
I’m asking because I’m lonely too.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.880
Para-sama…

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:59.810
It’s hot in here, isn’t it?

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:02.270
Then why don’t
we go where it’s cooler?

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:13.400
No change in the princess yet?

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.680
Unfortunately, no.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:19.070
It reminds me of the past.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.250
Like a certain someone, no?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:28.420
It’s not uncommon for a sibylla
to question her flight duties.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:34.240
I was the one who offered
you a helping hand then, right?

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.240
I haven’t forgotten.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.890
Vroom!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.050
Pow-pow-pow-pow!

00:14:40.050 --> 00:14:42.270
Vroom!

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.460
Vroom! Blam!

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.530
Pow-pow-pow-pow!
I see some more coming at us!

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:50.090
Blam! Pow-pow-pow-pow!

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:54.630
I’m not scared of that lame attack!
Let’s see you hit us if you can!

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:57.250
Vroom! Pow-pow-pow-pow!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.290
Hey! Para-sama!
Enemy to your right!

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:03.840
Strafe them with
the machine gun! Hurry!

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.880
All right!

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.440
Pow-pow-pow!

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.650
Wow, Para-sama! 100 of 100!

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:10.570
Pow-pow-pow! Pow-pow-pow-pow!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.890
Another group of enemies
beyond the clouds! Ray Ri Majon!

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.140
Kaim?

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:26.320
Hey, Para-sama…

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.120
Let’s do a Ri Majon.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:49.460
Strange… We always do that, but…

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.690
Uh-oh! We’ve got to turn it off!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:13.530
Kaim!

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.340
Big Sister…

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.260
Big Sister Kaim…

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.170
I was always by her side.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:11.670
I’d decided to stay by her side forever.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:16.930
And before I knew it, being near
her had become a natural thing.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.350
How arrogant of me…

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:35.990
Thinking I was the only
one she could ever lean on…

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.990
I thought that it was obvious…

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:54.010
In that moment,
I wasn’t the only one who felt pain.

00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:59.300
Is that the reason why?

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:10.230
Para-sama?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.310
Let’s not do this.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.270
Why?

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:15.540
Because you’re still a child, Kaim.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.470
What? I’m not a child!

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:18.460
You are.

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:19.780
I’m not!

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.570
We’re all children.

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:27.500
That’s why we try to heal our wounds
but end up creating new wounds.

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:32.550
I’m going now.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.410
Good night, Kaim.

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:41.780
Why?

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:46.980
Jeez, why can’t you
see how I feel, Para-sama?

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.610
Neviril!

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:04.150
Neviril! Just listen to me
for a second, will you?

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:05.830
Neviril!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.120
Neviril!

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.330
I swear…

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:16.340
Now that it’s come to this, I’ll drag
you out if it’s the last thing I do.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:18.870
Paraietta.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:21.380
Aer, I’d like to talk.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.940
It doesn’t look like we’re
about to do any talking.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.310
Didn’t you know?

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:35.940
The maju pool can
be used for this too.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:43.360
So how did I end up
having to face you like this?

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.120
Let’s go!

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:05.830
The reason Neviril refuses to decide
isn’t just because of Amuria.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:08.990
I see now.

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:12.810
It was also out of
respect for my feelings.

00:20:14.510 --> 00:20:19.030
Neviril, I’m sorry.
I didn’t know anything.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:23.600
But just let me say this.

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:27.740
I don’t feel as though
you’ve betrayed me!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.330
And I appreciate how
considerate you’re being.

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.040
That’s why…

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:40.630
That’s why…

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:47.340
That’s why I’ll put my hopes on
one who can surpass Amuria!

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.860
I’ve got you!

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.760
What?

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:03.990
Over here!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:11.980
You’re open!

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:12.970
What?

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.260
Is that good enough?

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.270
Aer! Go and pair up with Neviril!

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:45.860
You don’t have to tell me that.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:54.890
Hey, Floe…

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:56.620
What is it?

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.040
So what happens next?

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.320
What?

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:05.100
The birds who rest their wings…
You said they couldn’t fly forever.

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:07.590
They’ll fly again of course.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:08.800
They will?

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:13.490
That’s right. Because birds
were born to fly in the sky.

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:16.290
To fly in the sky…

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:23.520
If she’s resting her wings, it’s all right.

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:30.860
But a bird who can’t fly
because she’s been wounded…

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:32.950
…has no hope of survival.

00:22:41.230 --> 00:22:47.940
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.940 --> 00:22:52.180
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:59.250
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:06.950
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.740
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.740 --> 00:23:24.910
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.910 --> 00:23:28.920
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:38.790
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:44.340
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:47.800
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.800 --> 00:23:53.440
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.440 --> 00:23:59.560
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.080 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:07.920
In order to sign a peace treaty…

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:11.970
…delegations from the highlands and
the Arcus Prima are about to meet.

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.660
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>Over International Waters</b>

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.350
Over International Waters.
